# VEDA -- what goes into the public repository
#
# This file is an ALLOWLIST: it ignores everything, then names the software to
# include. It is written this way deliberately.
#
# This directory is a live research working directory, not a clean source tree.
# It currently holds, alongside the code:
#
#   runs_done/     19 GB of completed analyses (Hela_MHCI, lismo_april,
#                  run_for-proposal, TA_tau, TA_indi, ...)
#   data/          89 MB of in-progress output
#   *.xlsx         raw proteomics input and result workbooks
#   *.docx         a manuscript draft
#   resources/tools/  1.7 GB of third-party programs, five of them licensed
#                     to an individual and not redistributable
#
# A conventional "ignore the bad things" list was tried first and missed
# `data/` subfolders and `runs_done/` entirely -- directories that simply had
# not been thought of. The failure is one-directional and permanent: anything
# unanticipated gets published, git history cannot be edited afterwards
# without invalidating every clone, and what leaks is unpublished research.
#
# So the default is exclude, and each inclusion below is a deliberate choice.
# ADDING A NEW FILE TO THE REPO MEANS ADDING A LINE HERE. That is the point:
# the inconvenience is the safety mechanism.

# --- 1. Ignore everything at the top level ---------------------------------
/*

# --- 2. The software ------------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/INSTALL.md
!/install.sh
!/uninstall.sh
!/veda-doctor
!/veda-pack
!/src
!/installer
!/dashboard

# --- 3. resources/: the interface images, and the tools DOCUMENTATION only -
# The tools themselves are fetched by the installer and must never be
# committed. resources/tools/.gitignore repeats this locally.
!/resources
/resources/*
!/resources/*.png
!/resources/tools
/resources/tools/*
!/resources/tools/.gitignore
!/resources/tools/README.md
!/resources/tools/DTU_TOOLS.md

# --- 4. Never, even inside the directories above ---------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor/agent tooling that happens to live under src/.
#
# src/.claude/skills/ and src/.agents/skills/ hold symlinks into
# ~/.local/lib/pythonX.Y/site-packages/streamlit/.agents/skills/ -- Streamlit's
# own bundled skill, not part of VEDA. They must not be published:
#   * the link is relative and seven levels deep, so it only resolves from the
#     directory depth it was created at and breaks in any clone elsewhere;
#   * it points into ~/.local, which VEDA deliberately isolates itself from;
#   * it is local developer tooling, not something a researcher needs.
.claude/
.agents/
*.veda-orig
*.replaced-*
.DS_Store
._*
__MACOSX/

# veda_paths.json is generated per machine by the configure stage.
veda_paths.json

# Bundles built by veda-pack. A bundle without --free-only contains
# DTU-licensed programs and belongs only on access-controlled storage.
dist/

# A mirror URL can embed a token or name private infrastructure.
# installer/mirror.conf.example is committed in its place.
installer/mirror.conf

# --- Deliberately NOT included, and why ------------------------------------
#
#   setup.sh          An older installer that downloads and installs
#                     Miniconda and builds differently named environments.
#                     Publishing it would send researchers down a path that
#                     fights install.sh. The file is left on disk; it is
#                     simply not published.
#   requirements.txt  Not a pip requirements file -- it is a scratch note
#                     containing commands such as
#                     `conda remove -n deeptmhmm --all -y`. Harmful if a
#                     researcher pasted it. The real dependency specs are
#                     installer/envs/*.yml and *.pip.txt.
#   data/, runs_done/ Research data and results. See the note at the top.
#   *.xlsx, *.docx    Raw data and a manuscript draft.
#   logs/             Machine-local.
#
# To ship an example dataset, create an `examples/` directory with files
# chosen on purpose and add `!/examples` above. Do not un-ignore part of
# data/ or runs_done/ to do it.
